    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (76.54) and **Christian Yelich** (75.84) serving as our primary anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** remains the focal point of the lineup, boasting an elite 0.469 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Rocker, while **Christian Yelich** leverages a significant platoon advantage against the struggling Chandler (5.12 xERA). Additionally, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.81) earns a strong start despite a 39% rain risk; his leadoff positioning and the favorable matchup against Lodolo provide the high-ceiling production required to chase stolen bases, which remain our highest priority. While **Kyle Schwarber** (57.99) and **Trea Turner** (58.63) present solid mid-tier efficiency, the heavy lifting today falls on our outfield trio to capitalize on weak opposing arms and favorable batting order slots.\n\nRegarding bench construction, **Luke Raley** (44.34) was the most difficult exclusion from the active lineup. Despite a respectable projected output, the combination of a difficult matchup against Jax and park factors suppressed his efficiency just enough to keep him behind the production threshold of **Junior Caminero** (52.12) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (51.84). We are opting to sacrifice some of **Luke Raley**\u2019s utility to maintain the higher floor provided by **Junior Caminero** at the UTIL spot, even against the tough Gilbert. Caution is advised for both **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Lars Nootbaar** (55.37), as lingering precipitation risks in their respective venues could shorten their games; however, given the projected efficiency, we are proceeding with both in the starting rotation to maximize our daily cap usage.",
